ies, vitamins, or minerals; it's regulated globally as a food additive with permitted maximum levels."},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:antioxidant, en:preservative"},"e_number":{"en":"220"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q5282"}},"en:e223":{"name":{"en":"E223 - Sodium metabisulphite"},"description":{"en":"SODIUM METABISULFITE or sodium pyrosulfite -IUPAC spelling; Br. E. sodium metabisulphite or sodium pyrosulphite- is an inorganic compound of chemical formula Na2S2O5."},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:antioxidant, en:preservative"},"e_number":{"en":"223"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q284549"}},"en:e260":{"name":{"en":"E260 - Acetic acid"},"description":{"en":"ACETIC ACID, systematically named ethanoic acid, is a colourless liquid organic compound with the chemical formula CH3COOH -also written as CH3CO2H or C2H4O2-."},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:preservative"},"e_number":{"en":"260"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q47512"}},"en:e262":{"name":{"en":"E262 - Sodium acetates"},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:preservative, en:sequestrant"},"e_number":{"en":"262"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q339940"}},"en:e262i":{"name":{"en":"E262i - Sodium acetate"},"parents":["en:e262"],"description":{"en":"SODIUM ACETATE, also abbreviated NaOAc,[8] is the sodium salt of acetic acid."},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:preservative, en:sequestrant"},"e_number":{"en":"262"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q339940"}},"en:e262ii":{"name":{"en":"E262ii - Sodium diacetate"},"parents":["en:e262"],"additives_classes":{"en":"en:preservative, en:sequestrant"},"e_number":{"en":"262"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q409655"}},"en:e270":{"name":{"en":"E270 - Lactic acid"},"description":{"en":"An organic acid naturally occurring in fermented foods, first identified in sour milk, now produced globally through microbial fermentation. It's manufactured by fermenting carbohydrate sources like corn, sugarcane, or beets with lactic acid bacteria, followed by purification. Lactic acid has a sharp, tangy, sour taste and is used worldwide as an acidulant, preservative, and pH regulator in dairy products, baked goods, beverages, pickled vegetables, and processed meats. It also aids fermentation in foods like yogurt and sauerkraut. Nutritionally, it provides a negligible caloric contribution and no significant vitamins or minerals, functioning primarily as a flavoring and preservation agent rather than a nutrient source."},"wikidata":{"en":"Q56626856"}},"en:e281":{"name":{"en":"E281 - Sodium propionate"},"description":{"en":"Sodium propanoate or SODIUM PROPIONATE is the sodium salt of propionic acid."},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:preservative"},"e_number":{"en":"281"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q420130"}},"en:e282":{"name":{"en":"E282 - calcium propionate"},"description":{"en":"CALCIUM PROPIONATE has the formula Ca-C2H5COO-2. Calcium propionate is used as a preservative in a wide variety of products, including but not limited to:bread, other baked goods, processed meat, whey, and other dairy products."},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:preservative"},"e_number":{"en":"282"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q417394"}},"en:e296":{"name":{"en":"E296 - Malic acid"},"description":{"en":"MALIC ACID is an organic compound with the molecular formula C4H6O5. Malic acid has two stereoisomeric forms -L- and D-enantiomers-, though only the L-isomer exists naturally."},"e_number":{"en":"296"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q190143"}},"en:e297":{"name":{"en":"E297 - Fumaric acid"},"e_number":{"en":"297"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q139857"}},"en:e300":{"name":{"en":"E300 - Ascorbic acid"},"description":{"en":"Ascorbic acid is a naturally occurring organic compound found in citrus fruits, berries, and vegetables such as peppers and broccoli. Commercially, it is produced industrially through fermentation of glucose -often derived from corn-, followed by chemical conversion steps, yielding a highly pure, food-grade powder. It has a mildly tart, sour taste, similar to citrus. Ascorbic acid is widely used as a food additive -E300- for its antioxidant properties, preventing browning and preserving freshness in juices, canned goods, and processed foods. Nutritionally, it is an essential water-soluble vitamin, contributing to collagen synthesis, immune function, and iron absorption across diverse global diets."},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:antioxidant, en:sequestrant"},"e_number":{"en":"300"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q193598"}},"en:e301":{"name":{"en":"E301 - Sodium ascorbate"},"description":{"en":"SODIUM ASCORBATE is one of a number of mineral salts of ascorbic acid -vitamin C-."},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:antioxidant"},"e_number":{"en":"301"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q424551"}},"en:e304":{"name":{"en":"E304 - Fatty acid esters of ascorbic acid"},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:antioxidant"},"e_number":{"en":"304"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q43303953"}},"en:e304i":{"name":{"en":"E304i - Ascorbyl palmitate"},"parents":["en:e304"],"description":{"en":"ASCORBYL PALMITATE is an ester formed from ascorbic acid and palmitic acid creating a fat-soluble form of vitamin C."},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:antioxidant"},"e_number":{"en":"304"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q424521"}},"en:e306":{"name":{"en":"E306 - Tocopherol-rich extract"},"e_number":{"en":"306"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q141180"}},"en:e307":{"name":{"en":"E307 - Alpha-tocopherol"},"e_number":{"en":"307"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q158348"}},"en:e319":{"name":{"en":"E319 - Tertiary-butylhydroquinone (tbhq)"},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:antioxidant"},"e_number":{"en":"319"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q662443"}},"en:e320":{"name":{"en":"E320 - Butylated hydroxyanisole (bha)"},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:antioxidant"},"e_number":{"en":"320"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q409401"}},"en:e321":{"name":{"en":"E321 - Butylated hydroxytoluene"},"additives_classes":{"en":"en:antioxidant"},"e_number":{"en":"321"},"wikidata":{"en":"Q221945"}},"en:e322":{"name":{"en":"E322 - Lecithins"},"description":{"en":"is a generic term to designate any group of yellow-brownish fatty substances occurring in animal and plant tissues, and are used for smoothing food textures, dissolving powders -emulsif